From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: Network commands: listen on 127.0.0.1 only

With network_cmd_enable on, RetroArch took commands on UDP port 55355 from
any host, without authentication: QUIT, LOAD_STATE, WRITE_CORE_RAM and the
rest. Worse, in v1.22.2 READ_CORE_RAM overflows the heap on a large byte
count (upstream fa49a43dc2), so one packet from the network could corrupt
memory of a process running as ark, who has sudo. "Enable Quick Mode"
turns network commands on, because it closes RetroArch with
`retroarch --command QUIT`, which sends to localhost.

The command socket now binds to 127.0.0.1: local senders such as Quick
Mode work as before, and nothing reaches it from the network.

diff --git a/command.c b/command.c
index 791d510547..bdc26f30d8 100644
--- a/command.c
+++ b/command.c
@@ -239,7 +239,7 @@ command_t* command_network_new(uint16_t port)
    command_t            *cmd = (command_t*)calloc(1, sizeof(*cmd));
    command_network_t *netcmd = (command_network_t*)calloc(
                                    1, sizeof(command_network_t));
-   int fd = socket_init((void**)&res, port, NULL,
+   int fd = socket_init((void**)&res, port, "127.0.0.1",
          SOCKET_TYPE_DATAGRAM, AF_INET);
 
    RARCH_LOG("[NetCMD] %s %hu.\n",
